---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import prompt from '../../docs/RESEARCH_SESSION_PROTOCOL_PROMPT.md?raw';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const internal = (segment) => `${base}/${segment.replace(/^\//, '')}`;
---
<Layout title="Memory Palace Protocol" description="The Agalmic Research Memory Palace Protocol v0.2 for provenance, epistemic authority, search-space mapping and decision replay across research sessions.">
  <header class="page-head">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Research operating protocol · v0.2</p>
      <h1>A memory palace for the research process.</h1>
      <p class="lede">A platform-agnostic session prompt for preserving how knowledge emerged: contribution, authority, evidence, alternatives, roads not taken, decisions, gaps and the graph transitions that connect them.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button" href={internal('downloads/Agalmic_Research_Memory_Palace_Protocol_v0.2.md')} download>Download Markdown</a>
        <a class="button secondary" href="https://github.com/TsatsuAmable/agalmicresearch/blob/main/docs/RESEARCH_SESSION_PROTOCOL_PROMPT.md">View canonical source ↗</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Governing distinction</p>
        <h2>Do not confuse contribution with authority.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="large">The protocol treats each research session as a directed, versioned graph of discovery rather than a flat transcript.</p>
        <div class="callout"><p><strong>Origin deserves credit. Authority requires warrant.</strong></p></div>
        <p>It records what was explored, selected, rejected, deferred, surfaced but unexamined and excluded by scope, while explicitly refusing to pretend that unknown alternatives were considered.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Short activation</p>
        <h2>Use this when the full protocol is already available to the researcher or agent.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <blockquote class="activation">Activate the Agalmic Research Memory Palace Protocol v0.2. Treat this session as a versioned graph of discovery. Track contribution provenance separately from epistemic authority; capture material questions, concepts, claims, evidence, objections, decisions and artefacts; preserve explored, rejected, deferred, surfaced-but-unexamined and scope-excluded branches; record reversal conditions and search boundaries; flag epistemic handoffs and publication/IP boundaries; and at closeout produce the complete Research Memory Palace Packet plus machine-readable graph patch. Do not infer expertise or attribution without evidence, do not treat absent alternatives as rejected, and do not request or fabricate hidden chain-of-thought.</blockquote>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="section-number">Canonical prompt</span>
        <div class="section-copy">
          <h2>The complete operating protocol.</h2>
          <p>This page renders the repository source directly. The displayed protocol and canonical Markdown therefore share the same source object.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <pre class="protocol-text">{prompt}</pre>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Related infrastructure</p>
        <h2>The prompt feeds the research graph.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Each provenance-complete session should end with a Research Memory Palace Packet and a machine-readable graph patch that can extend the project-wide discovery graph.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button" href={internal('provenance')}>Explore provenance</a>
          <a class="button secondary" href={internal('research-graph.json')}>Research graph JSON</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .protocol-text {
      white-space: pre-wrap;
      overflow-wrap: anywhere;
      border: 1px solid var(--rule, #c9c4b8);
      padding: clamp(1rem, 2vw, 2rem);
      font: 0.9rem/1.55 ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, "Liberation Mono", monospace;
      background: rgba(255,255,255,0.28);
      max-width: 100%;
      overflow-x: auto;
    }
    .activation {
      margin: 0;
      padding-left: 1rem;
      border-left: 3px solid currentColor;
    }
  </style>
</Layout>
